Caelza: the Mind turned on from the Memory page (vision M3, no shell): the
gateway's api_mind_install.rs (an overlay module) does what
mind/windows-install.ps1 and mind/install.sh do as a background job the
page watches (the release's tarball checked against its .sha256, a
portable Node from nodejs.org when none new enough is on PATH, npm install,
the launcher, the tokens, the service started), so the PC path has no
PowerShell step left. These hunks register the module and its routes and list the page logic
test beside the others.
Applied after 0016 and the overlay copy.

--- a/crates/caelza-gateway/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/caelza-gateway/src/lib.rs
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 pub mod api_logs;
